# PE TimeDateStamp for the Windows native libraries, in Unix seconds.
#
# One value for both architectures, written into the COFF header and the export
# directory by patch-pe-timestamp.py after the link. It lives in the repository
# on purpose: a value derived from the build (HEAD commit time, environment) would
# change whenever any file changes, including Java-only commits that leave the
# DLL bytes identical — and Smart App Control / Defender key their reputation on
# the file hash, so a moving timestamp restarts it on every release.
#
# Bump it only when the native sources change:
#   prebuilt/bump-pe-timestamp.sh
# and commit the result together with the native change.
1794355675
